hip is weaker. In general, though, assessing the strength of a relationship just by looking at the scatterplot is quite problematic, and we need a numerical measure to help us with that. We will discuss that later in this section.","position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"key":"ryy3uIs6MZ"}],"key":"FA9AmAukYB"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Outliers","position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"key":"c5Et5fZOv7"}],"identifier":"outliers","label":"Outliers","html_id":"outliers","implicit":true,"key":"lQbOzhxZtL"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Data points that ","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"key":"dRLqJgYM7R"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"deviate from the pattern","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"key":"wlPT5bZ7Rb"}],"key":"WIgnqJxMjG"},{"type":"text","value":" of the relationship are called ","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"key":"Rvpb52LWeK"},{"type":"crossReference","label":"outlier","identifier":"term-outlier","children":[{"type":"text","value":"outliers","key":"z1QeXfzcns"}],"kind":"definitionTerm","template":"{name}","resolved":true,"html_id":"term-outlier","remote":true,"url":"/pages/glossary","dataUrl":"/pages.glossary.json","key":"ctp86zI2Om"},{"type":"text","value":". We will see several examples of outliers during this section. Two outliers are illustrated in the scatterplot below:","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"key":"ncN0hy8lH0"}],"key":"VNdXM7M2wi"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/textbook/